 "fan_kg": 1073.0,
 "intro": "<p>Two runs of the car as built, at 180 km/h over a moving road with the wheels turning: once with the fans stopped, once with them drawing 8 m\u00b3/s out of the sealed floor, as the spec says they do. The first attempt at the second run found the fans could not breathe at all: their intakes opened onto the track, two millimetres from it, and the road shut them. They now open in the tunnel roofs, and the car was rebuilt before the run below.</p>",
 "caption": "Fans running. The deep blue under the floor is the plenum they hold under suction; the orange on the nose and the wings' leading edges is where the air stops against them.",
 "notes": [
  [
   "The fans are the car",
   "Stopped, they leave the sealed floor full of air rammed in at the nose, and it lifts: +2.1 m\u00b2. Running, they pull it down to 4.7 m\u00b2 of downforce, most of the car's total. The spec had it the other way round: the floor's downforce as a given, the fans on top."
  ],
  [
   "The wings do better than claimed",
   "Front and rear together make 1.67 m\u00b2 with the fans off and 1.93 with them on, against the 1.2 the spec gave them. The rear wing is also the largest single source of drag."
  ],
  [
   "The balance is further aft",
   "With the fans running 32 % of the downforce is on the front axle, not the 44.5 % the spec and the lap simulation assume: the fans pull hardest at the back of the floor, where their intakes are."
  ]
 ],
